# Fixed 2026-10-08, defect 477, lane b15-check (class improvement).
# Symptom: a call of n arguments cost the checker faster than n: whether a
# parameter's type is shared, which decides whether its argument is named
# (spec § 4.9), was asked of each position against every other, at the
# call, at the callee's own type and at a type written; and each argument
# asked the list of shared positions, and of labels the call writes.
# Cause: four copies of one pairwise question, and lists asked by scanning.
# `type_fit.shared` counts each type once for a whole run, and each label
# check asks a set. This case: a function of 802 parameters, 800 of one
# type, called with one label missing, two swapped and two missing; a call
# through a value of a named type; a written type left unnamed; and a
# construction with a label naming nothing and a label missing.

